## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses the ability to translate regulatory requirements into automated, auditable technical controls using Azure AI and governance services, with strict multi-tenant isolation requirements.

## Key Concepts

- Regulatory-to-controls mapping (GDPR/CCPA/NIST)
- Knowledge base grounding with Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant RBAC and data isolation
- Automated evidence collection and auditable logging
- Azure Policy integration for continuous enforcement

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: Map obligations to controls and enforce per-tenant policy
async function ensureCompliance(clientId) {
  const obligations = await kb.fetchObligations(clientId);
  const controls = await mapToControls(obligations);

  const evidence = await collectEvidence(clientId, controls);
  const violations = await evaluateAgainstPolicy(controls, evidence);

  await logDecision({ clientId, obligations, controls, evidence, violations });
  return generateRemediationPlan(violations);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a comprehensive Azure OpenAI solution that integrates multiple Azure services while addressing key enterprise requirements like multilingual support, data governance, and cost management in a beginner-friendly scenario.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and per-tenant language preference management
- Per-language knowledge bases stored in Azure Blob Storage
- Real-time translation layer and content grounding via Azure Cognitive Search
- PII redaction and per-tenant budget enforcement mechanisms
- API Management routing policies and comprehensive auditing to Azure Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: detect language, translate, search knowledge base, query OpenAI, translate back
const lang = detectLanguage(request);
const kb = await loadLanguageKB(lang);
const translatedQuery = await translateToEnglish(request, lang);
const groundedContext = await cognitiveSearch(translatedQuery, kb);
const response = await callOpenAI(groundedContext);
return translateFromEnglish(response, lang);
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement currency and locale handling while ensuring no PII leakage across language translations?
- How would you scale this architecture to handle multiple tenants with different language support requirements?

## Why This Is Asked

Assess ability to design a secure, scalable retrieval-augmented reviewer with per-tenant isolation, governance, and observability for code and IaC changes.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant KB
- Retrieval-Augmented Generation with Cognitive Search
- PII/secret redaction via Text Analytics and Key Vault
- Policy engine to block leakage
- Canary rollout behind API Management
- Auditing and data lineage in Data Lake

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: route a prompt with redaction and policy check
async function handleRequest(req){
  const payload = redactPII(req.payload);
  if(!policyAllows(payload)) throw new Error('Blocked');
  const ans = await openai.request({prompt: payload, ...req.options});
  logAudit(req, ans);
  return ans;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test leakage prevention and ensure zero cross-tenant data exposure?
- What metrics and limits would you set for latency, cost, and data-plane guardrails?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests knowledge of Azure OpenAI integration, policy-based gating, and tenant isolation in a practical chat app.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-policy retrieval from Azure Key Vault
- Input screening with Azure Text Analytics
- Policy gating before Azure OpenAI calls
- Grounding with Cognitive Search and KB in Blob
- Per-tenant auditing to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
async function handle(input, tenantId){
  const policy = await fetchPolicy(tenantId)
  if(!passesPolicy(input, policy)) return cannedReply(policy)
  const grounded = groundKB(input)
  return await openAiQuery(grounded)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test different policy rules per tenant?
- How would you handle policy updates without redeploying services?"

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design end-to-end Azure OpenAI-powered data-governance tooling that handles multi-tenant isolation, secure KB grounding, and robust testing.

## Key Concepts
- Data lineage ingestion and normalization across Synapse/Data Factory.
- Versioned KB in Azure Blob and Cognitive Search integration.
- Per-tenant isolation with Key Vault-backed Cosmos DB storage.
- Prompt engineering with fallback chains and confidence scoring.
- Data redaction and auditability.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for gap-filling using KB
async function fillLineageGap(partialLineage, kbClient) {
  if (partialLineage.isComplete()) return partialLineage;
  const kb = await kbClient.query(partialLineage.pattern);
  return partialLineage.enrich(kb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure the accuracy of enrichment?
- How would you handle cycles or conflicting KB results?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Azure OpenAI deployment, API management, knowledge-grounding, data privacy, and governance in a realistic, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Service integration with gateway
- Knowledge-grounding via Azure Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- Per-repo policy gating and audit logging to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redactPII and gate before OpenAI call
function handleRequest(req){
  const redacted = redactPII(req.input);
  if (!policyAllows(req.repo, redacted)) return denyResponse();
  return callOpenAI({input:redacted});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate per-repo gating with mock sensitive files?
- How would you extend to support multiple KB sources and versioning nuances?

## Why This Is Asked
To assess hands-on Azure AI wiring for accessibility use cases, including voice input, multilingual output, and privacy controls, all grounded in a managed KB.

## Key Concepts
- Azure API Management as a gate
- Azure OpenAI with grounding to a versioned KB in Blob via Cognitive Search
- Azure Speech to Text and Text to Speech
- Per-tenant language preferences
- PII redaction and interaction logging

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example flow tying services together
async function handleQuery(audioBlob, language) {
  const text = await speechToText(audioBlob, language);
  const answer = await openai.chat({ messages: [{ role: 'user', content: text }] });
  const tts = await textToSpeech(answer.choices[0].message.content, language);
  return tts;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model per-tenant language settings in Cosmos DB?
- What are the trade-offs between cloud TTS and on-device synthesis for accessibility tasks?
